[246.167508, "o", "Created `/app/polyglot/main.py.c`.\r\n\r\nIt works with both commands:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\npython3 /app/polyglot/main.py.c 100\r\ngcc /app/polyglot/main.py.c -o /app/polyglot/cmain && /app/polyglot/cmain 100\r\n```\r\n\r\nBoth print:\r\n\r\n```text\r\n354224848179261915075\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe C side uses arbitrary-precision integer arithmetic, so it does not overflow for larger `N`, and the Python side handles Python 3.12’s large-integer string conversion limit.\r\n"]
